    "description": "Tests in real browsers through Chrome DevTools MCP: inspects the DOM, captures console errors, analyzes network requests, profiles performance and verifies visual output with runtime data. Use this skill when: building or debugging anything that runs in a browser. Do NOT use this skill when: only writing Playwright test code without runtime inspection (use automating-browser-tests).",
    "prompt": "Ative e aplique a skill `lay-testing-in-browser-with-devtools` para este escopo. Siga rigorosamente as instruções da fonte `LAY® Core Ecosystem` mantendo comunicação concisa (Caveman) e validação baseada em evidências.",
    "content": "# Browser Testing with DevTools\n\n## Sections\n- Overview\n- When to Use\n- Setting Up Chrome DevTools MCP\n- Security Boundaries\n- The DevTools Debugging Workflow\n- Writing Test Plans for Complex UI Bugs\n- Screenshot-Based Verification\n- Console Analysis Patterns\n- Accessibility Verification with DevTools\n- Common Rationalizations\n- Red Flags\n- Verification\n\n## Reference Documentation\nConsulte a documentação técnica completa: [Referência Técnica](reference.md).",
